            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="0999" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2963: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-07T15:00:00+02:35">December 7, 1935—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 7—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>211. My 209, December 6, 4 p.m. Have not yet heard from American mission at
                    Dessie direct but from official version and reports from American newspapermen
                    it appears that some 40 incendiary and explosive bombs were dropped on American
                    mission and hospital compound of which 5 hit hospital building wrecking 2 rooms.
                    Norwegian nurse there broke leg jumping into trench for shelter. All others
                    including some 65 patients and American journalists on grounds had miraculous
                    escape. Injured Norwegian nurse was brought to Addis Ababa by plane today.
                    Unconfirmed report states one Belgian officer and one French journalist wounded
                    and about 40 natives dead and 100 wounded.</p>
                <p>Difficult to understand why American hospital should have been bombed as it lies
                    outside city, is easily distinguishable by red crosses painted on roofs, had
                    very large American flag flying and there were several ambulances with red
                    crosses painted on tops standing near, one of which is reported to have been
                    destroyed.</p>
                <p>Have just learned Dessie was again bombed this morning but no details available
                    as yet.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
